Create and run your first project (same commands on Windows and macOS):
```bash
flutter create my_first_lao_app
cd my_first_lao_app
flutter devices
flutter run
```

A cleaner starter `lib/main.dart` example:
```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

void main() => runApp(const MyApp());

class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const MyApp({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp(
      home: Scaffold(
        appBar: AppBar(title: const Text('First Lao Flutter App')),
        body: Center(
          child: Column(
            mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.center,
            children: [
              const Text('ສະບາຍດີ! (Hello!)'),
              const SizedBox(height: 20),
              ElevatedButton(
                onPressed: () => debugPrint('Button Pressed!'),
                child: const Text('Click Me'),
              ),
            ],
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

Platform-specific run commands:
```bash
# Android (works on both Windows and macOS)
flutter run -d <android-device-id>

# iOS (macOS only)
flutter run -d <ios-device-id>
```
Get device IDs from `flutter devices`. On Windows, the iOS option will not appear — that is normal.

`WHERE` filters rows for `SELECT`, `UPDATE`, and `DELETE`.

:::defs
**= / !=**|Equal / not equal
**> / >=**|Greater than (or equal)
**BETWEEN a AND b**|Inclusive range
**LIKE 'A%'**|Pattern match (`%` = any suffix)
**AND / OR**|Combine conditions
:::

Examples:
```sql
SELECT * FROM users WHERE age = 24;
SELECT * FROM users WHERE age BETWEEN 20 AND 30;
SELECT * FROM users WHERE name LIKE 'A%';
SELECT * FROM users WHERE age > 20 AND name LIKE 'A%';
SELECT * FROM users WHERE age < 22 OR age > 27;
```
